{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed them.</b> And likewise: ״ויברך אלהים את יום השביעי״. Thus you learn that one who acquires a new thing recites the blessing shehecheyanu." "<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> But mules were not included in the blessing, as we say: ״הוא ענה, אשר מצא את הימים במדבר״ — and therefore they are not fruitful and do not multiply in the world. And even according to Rabbi Yose, who concludes in the chapter מקום שנהגו that at the close of the Sabbath of creation Adam brought two animals and mated one upon the other and a mule came out of them — there is no difficulty at all, for 'be fruitful and multiply' was said before."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:49.172208864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}